{"title":"5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Five is an integer. In integers it belongs to the set of prime . It is sum of two smallest squares of distinct natural numbers. \n5 has a pretty nice divisibility rule . If the one's place of any integer in 0 or 5 , then the integer is divisible by 5. \n5 is also a prime, which means it is only divisible by 1 and itself\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=5&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018071542\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.005 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.009 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 7/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 244/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.304      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.304      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:30855:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018071542 and revision id 288954. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}